From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CDDA Web Publisher <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:05:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Use OpenGL ES renderer in browser

Emscripten's SDL3 port provides the opengles2 renderer, not the desktop
opengl renderer.  Include it as the accelerated fallback after SDL's GPU
renderer so browser builds use WebGL instead of silently dropping to the
software renderer.
---
 src/sdltiles.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sdltiles.cpp b/src/sdltiles.cpp
index cb757688ed..242e737c2e 100644
--- a/src/sdltiles.cpp
+++ b/src/sdltiles.cpp
@@ -618,6 +618,8 @@ static void WinCreate()
         dbg( D_INFO ) << "Only SPIR-V shader artifacts present; biasing the "
                       "GPU device toward Vulkan.";
     }
+#  elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+    SDL_SetHint( SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER, "gpu,opengles2" );
 #  else
     SDL_SetHint( SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER, "gpu,opengl" );
 #  endif
